(The story so far ....  No, just kidding ...)

Back on 25 I pick up as much as I can carry and go down to 26.  There is a
statue of a fire giant in the foyer but its presence is inconclusive.  I
drop stuff and then cautiously explore the level relying upon my helm of
telepathy to warn me of Medusa's proximity.  I encounter a small beehive and
three lumps of royal jelly push my strength a little higher.  A swirly
potion makes me feel enlightened and I discover the following about myself:

	Current Attributes:

	You are stridently aligned.
	You can teleport.
	You aggravate monsters.
	You are poison resistant.
	You are cold resistant.
	You are shock resistant.
	You are sleep resistant.
	You are protected.
	You have teleport control.
	You are telepathic.
	You are fast.
	You are invisible.
	You are magic-protected.
	You have extra luck.
	Good luck does not time out for you.

Oh disaster!  While exploring I step on a trapdoor!  I am now on level 27 in
a maze.  That makes it almost certain that Medusa is on level 26 waiting for
me at the top of the stairs.  "So what?" you ask.  Well, muggins doesn't
have his potion of blindness!  I dropped it along with all the other stuff
in the foyer of level 26.  Oh woe!  Oh stupidity!  Why, why, why did I go
exploring?  Surely if I had fetched all my stuff from upstairs I would have
picked up the potion of blindness before exploring the level!  How could I
have been so bloody stupid?

Oh well, no point brooding about it.  Job now is to find the stairs in each
direction.  If I can't find a means of making myself blind I must hope to
find a level teleporter so I can come back down from level 25.  A minautor
succumbs to Stormbringer and the wand of digging will make it easier to move
around.  There is a dwarf king here chopping away at the walls so I leave him
to it.

I beat up a few soldier ants whose corpses don't do anything for me, then,
joy of joys, a flesh golem corpse gives me a momentary chill!  I didn't know
they were hot creatures.  So at last I have intrinsic fire resistance and do
not have to rely on the ring!  To offset that advantage I stumble onto a
rust trap and my helm of telepathy loses one point of protection.

After a teleport-gone-awry (presumably because I tried to land on a trap,
monster or boulder), I find the stairs leading upwards.  The temptation to
climb is easy to resist!  Another teleport opportunity shows that there was
indeed a boulder at the location I had previously selected.  (Still no sign
of a tengu anywhere.  I have only seen one throughout the entire game so I
am still having to rely on my ring for teleport control.)  I see a couple of
frost giants but I have no appetite just now so I am in no hurry to deal
with them .... hang on a moment .... what about my tinning kit?  Yes, I do
have it with me.  Well that could come in handy.  I refrain from putting on
my calorie-consuming ring of regeneration and continue exploring.  Another
teleport opportunity and I opt to move near the giants.  I am not carrying
any potions and I am cold-resistant.  A few moments later I have a couple of
tins of frost giant meat.  Furthermore, I have found the stairs leading down-
wards.  I bash up some more beasts and find a magic trap but no level tele-
porter.  Munching on a tin of frost giant meat my strength goes from 18/27
to 18/34 but the meat is rotten and for a while I am stunned and confused.
I try the unicorn horn again.  My confusion vanishes and my steadiness
returns!  Maybe that unicorn horn is a panacea of sorts?  There is a nurse
nearby but I have 99 hit points and I am not sure I can be bothered screwing
for more.  Maybe if she can be lured into a cul-de-sac I'll undress for her
but I shan't waste too much time.  I discover a teleportation trap but it is
not the level-shifting variety.  Pooh.  Nurse follows me into a blind alley
but I discover I cannot undress fully because my +4 helm of telepathy is
still cursed so I zap my way out and leave her to her frustrations.

By this time I have explored most of the maze although the activities of the
dwarf king are making it difficult for me to keep track of what I have seen
in his domain so I clobber him and the other beasts nearby.  I see plenty of
potions and traps but nothing of value.  I guess it is time to go down.

No, 28 is a normal level.  Hearing blades being honed I suspect there is a
barracks on this level.  Unfortunately none of the soldiers is carrying a
potion of blindness.  There are two chests in the barracks but I notice an
unintelligible inscription on the ground.  A bit of searching locates a door
and a bit more searching reveals a LEVEL TELEPORTER!  Yippee!  While I am
here I take the opportunity to investigate the chests.  Kicking them open
I find that one is empty but the other contains a cursed potion of healing
(which I elect to leave there).

While here I can't resist a peek downstairs.  Level 29 is a maze, not the
castle level.  I have no particular interest in lingering but decide to look
for the stairs downward.  In the process I discover a magic lamp!  I elect
to leave it there for later because it is not blessed and I don't have any
holy water with me.  On second thoughts I pick it up.  I plan to carry it
back to level 25 and use it there.  Abandoning my explorations I take the
next teleport back to the stairs and climb them, head for the barracks and
the level teleporter, remove my cloak of protection and my dragon suit and
take a ride to level 25.  I grab as many potions of holy water as I can
carry and head downstairs to the pile of stuff on level 26.  I use one
holy water to bless the magic lamp and ask for three blessed scrolls of
charging.  I only get one.  Now what?  I have lots of blank paper, a blessed
magic marker with unknown chargeability and a wand of wishing with an unknown
number of charges.  Try the magic marker?  Risky.  What if, like the others,
it doesn't charge?  Recharge the lamp?  Also risky because there is no
guarantee that I'd get more than one scroll next time.  Try the wand of
wishing?  Maybe.  Zapping the wand of wishing a few times yields the
"Nothing happens" message.  That probably means its former owner had used up
the first three wishes and was carrying it around in the hope of recharging
it later.  This seems promising so I read the charging scroll and my wand of
wishing glows blue for a moment.  I zap it and ask for 3 blessed scrolls of
charging.  This time I get them.  I use one on the magic marker but nothing
happens so I throw the marker away.  Now I'm really glad I didn't waste the
first one!

Now what?  I figure I have at most four wishes left, three from the wand and
one from the lamp.  I'd like to genocide all the liches because they have a
tendency to curse things.  I'd also like to either get rid of rust monsters
or rustproof my battle gear.  It would also be nice to summon some tengus,
wraiths and nurses (in that order of preference) so some cursed scrolls of
genocide would be handy.  Then of course I could always use some higher
characteristics, particularly intelligence.  Other useful things would be
boots or a ring of levitation, some scrolls of enchant armour and some
spellbooks of identify.  

In summary, my wishes include:

	3 blessed potions of gain ability
	3 blessed scrolls of genocide
	3 cursed scrolls of genocide
	a high-quality blessed magic marker
	other stuff of lesser inportance

I expect there'll be a wand of wishing on the castle level so I can worry
about it all again later.

The three potions of gain ability push my unaugmented dexterity to 16, cons-
titution to 18, intelligence and charisma to 17.  I only get one blessed
scroll of genocide which I use to delete all liches, master liches and demi-
liches.  I only get one cursed scroll of genocide but for the moment I
refrain from reading it.  My reasoning is that I am going to ask for tengus
in the hope of gaining intrinsic teleport control but I don't know if I have
to remove my ring first and I'd hate to be random-teleported into the same
room as Medusa.  So picking up the potion of blindness I go hunting, very,
very carefully.  I skirt around rooms containing a rust monster and a gnome
of some sort, single-stepping along the corridors.  As I approach the right
hand side of the dungeon I see a green humanesque symbol.  Yes, it is the
snake lady herself.  Quaff that potion.  Wield Stormbringer.  March boldly
up to Medusa and chop her to death.  Well done, Sir!

I crack open all the statues on this level with my pick-axe but none yields
anything interesting so I retreat to a quiet corner to summon some tengus.
I get four.  Each leaves a corpse but eating the corpses does not give me
intrinsic teleport control.  One of them makes me blind but forgetting that
condition I nevertheless read my scroll of charging.  My magic lamp vibrates
briefly.  Did it charge?  I apply my unicorn horn (a bit late) and #rub the
lamp.  Sure enough, I get another cursed scroll of genocide.  I ask for
tengus again.  Four more are sent in but not one leaves a corpse.  I do get
a potion of levitation which will help on the castle level.

Having used up my four wishes with moderate effect it is time to head down
towards hell.  Wait a minute!  There are two tengus nearby.  I track one of
them down but it leaves no corpse.  I encounter a couple of hill giants and
eat one for strength and nourishment, bless my tinning kit and use it on the
other giant.  Picking up as much as I can carry I descend to level 27 and
head downstairs.  On the way I fall through a trapdoor and end up on level
29.  Climbing back to 28 I start preparations for a polypile in the barracks
by gathering all the armour into three colinear heaps.  I also deposit some
useless scrolls, potions and spellbooks.  I'm not going to be able to hit
the piles very much; what I am looking to obtain is a pair of boots or a
ring which will give me levitation ability.  (I don't trust my ability to
cast spells and I'll probably need to traverse the corridor on the castle
level more than once.)

Back up on 27 (the maze level) I still have not located the upwards stairs
so I have quite a bit of exploration to do.  I find a tengu (who obviously
fell through the trapdoor from above) but eating its corpse still does not
give me teleport control.  It does however leave behind a flute and since
the harp I fetched from level 7 is still cursed I take the flute with me.


The nurse is in a blind alley but dalliance only pushes my hit points up
from 99 to 101.  I find the upward stairs underneath a pile of stuff.  I
guess I did locate them earlier and just hid them from myself.  Hmph.  To
make things easy for myself I dig a direct channel between the two stair-
cases.

Down on 28 I head for the barracks skirting a rust monster.  On the way
back the rust monster is blocking my passage so I take a chance and wield
Mjollnir which I suspect is rustproof.  Sure enough, I clobber the rust
monster and my war hammer named Mjollnir is not affected.

One zap with the wand of polymorph and I get two unidentified spellbooks
on the first pile.  The first of these turns out to be identify and the
second, invisibility.  Neither of two pairs of boots lifts me up and none
of the rings is unidentified.  Stepping to the second pile I see a sapphire
ring and a cursed diamond ring.  The sapphire ring produces no immediate
effect so I drop it again.  There is nothing else of value in the pile so
carrying my diamond ring I head to the top of the stairs where I have left
my holy water.  I #dip the ring and put it on; I float in the air!

Well now I have achieved what I hoped for out of the polypile exercise with
just one zap.  My wand of polymorph has only the hidden charge left in it
which I manage to extract after only about twenty zaps.  The first pile
now has a blessed scroll called ELBIB YLOH which I am tempted to read.
First, however, I take off a lot of my armour because I have not yet seen
a scroll of enchant armour and I do not want my good gear evaporating.
The precautions turn out to be a waste of time because the scroll is one
of create monster.  The third pile has a light blue spellbook but it is
just one of "detect unseen" and not very interesting.  I pick up a scroll
of identify, two potions of enlightenment and from the pile and a wand which
has become a wand of polymorph.
 
I am not very interested in waving the new polymorph wand because I haven't
many scrolls, spellbooks or potions and they are really the only interesting
things to polymorph now.  However I succumb to temptation and pile three
yields a scroll called NR 9 which turns out to be enchant armour.

Abandoning what is left in the piles I head down to level 29 which I have
only partly explored, then immediately to 30 where I hear the tones of
courtly conversation before stepping straight down to 31 which is obviously
the castle level.  Dropping every unnecessary item I return to level 30 to
tackle the throne room.  From a short distance I can see that the room holds
six dragons, an ettin, some orcs and bugbears, a centaur and a couple of
trolls.  Time for the ring of conflict!  Stormbringer seems the better
weapon against the dragons but I don't encounter much resistance.  To keep
the trolls from self-reincarnating I tin them.  It seems to work.  I wonder
if I can do that to the Wizard of Yendor?

There is another hidden door in the throne room and it leads to a level
teleporter.  Bluish-orange fumes billow from the chest as I open it and my
vision blurs.  The unicorn horn puts that right!  A truly amazing item,
although I don't know that I can afford to carry it far into hell.  The
chest yields a glowing spellbook which turns out to be one of cancellation.

I #sit on the throne.  I feel out of place.  I #sit again.  "You may wish
for an object.  What do you want?"  Un-bloody-believable.  Shall I try for
tengus again?  I ask for 2 cursed scrolls of genocide and get them.  The
throne vanishes in a puff of Douglas Adams logic.  In a quiet room away from
trapdoors and teleporters I read the first scroll.  Of six tengus four leave
a corpse but eating the bodies does nothing.  Second scroll produces five
tengus of which two leave corpses.  On eating the first of these I feel in
control of myself.  About bloody time!  I wonder if it was really worth the
trouble.  Picking up the food rations scattered around I head for the
castle level.

I map out the small maze at the near end and in front of the castle deposit
the useful things in one pile and the junk in another.  Note that my ring of
teleport control is now a junk item.  I bless my two potions of enlighten-
ment before quaffing because I could use the extra point of intelligence.

Well here I am on the castle level with only one means of opening the front
door.  In all previous visits I have had a spellbook of knock or a wand of
opening which lowers the drawbridge easily.  I am not sure what to do with
the flute but I do know it is a means of opening the gate.

I apply the flute.  "Improvise?", Nethack asks.  I say "yes" and I "start
playing the flute".  After a few such attempts nothing interesting has
happened so I answer "no" to the "improvise" question.  This time Nethack
asks me "What tune are you playing? [what 5 notes]"  Aha!  This is that
5-note Mastermind game that I've seen mentioned on Usenet.

   aaaaa     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   bbbbb     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   ccccc     You extract a strange sound from the flute

This isn't very promising.  What does this mean?

   ddddd     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   cdefg     You extract a strange sound from the flute

What is going on here?  Perhaps I am too far away from the gate.  I move
to the point directly across the moat and try again.

   cdefg     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear 1 tumbler click and 2 gears turn

Not sure what the tumbler and gear sounds mean yet.  I suspect that I can't
draw any conclusion from my previous attempts so I start the process all
over again.

   aaaaa     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   bbbbb     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   ccccc     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear 2 gears turn

OK!  So gear sounds mean a note in the correct place in the sequence.  Let's
find out where the Cs are.

   cccaa     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear one tumbler click and one gear turn

So one of the Cs is in one of the last two positions

   aaaac     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear 1 gear turn

Got it!  I have a hunch that the first position is also a C

   caaac     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear 2 gears turn

Fine.  Now for the middle three notes.

   cdddc     You extract a strange sound from the flute
   ceeec     You extract a strange sound from the flute

Only Fs and Gs left

   cfffc     You extract a strange sound from the flute
             You hear 4 gears turn

One of the middle 3 is a G

   cgffc     You extract a strange sound from the flute
	     You see a drawbridge coming down!

Lucky!  It was the first of the three.

I drop the flute on the pile of junk before heading into the castle.  The
soldiers guarding the entrance present no challenge and the denizens of the
throne room succumb to a combination of Mjollnir and their own in-fighting
(induced by my ring of conflict).  From the chest behind the throne I pull
a scroll of enchant weapon.  There's an umber hulk corpse here so I have
a chance to rustproof Stormbringer.  I eat the corpse but it doesn't make
me confused.  Oops.  I was wrong about that.  The throne vanishes in a
puff of logic as I sit on it.  I can see a grey dragon in the lower chamber
behind the throne.  I head for the northern parapet and deal with the guards.
Nothing interesting in either tower so I enter the southern ramparts.  The
eastern tower has two soldiers guarding a wand of wishing.  Note that I still
have my blessed scroll of charging so if all goes well I could get another
seven wishes.  I have only three potions of holy water left and I use one to
bless the wand of wishing because I think that a blessed wand has a better
chance of not missing wishes.  Of course I don't actually know if that is
true.

Decisions, decisions.  What do I want or need now?  Perhaps a Hawaiian shirt?
An amulet of life-saving?  (Can I get an amulet of life-saving by wishing
for it?)  While wondering I decide to zap my wand of polymorph at my pile of
useless items.  After one zap I remember the chest and carry it from the
throne room to the pile.  Also there is a leash in one of the piles left
behind by the soldiers so I drop that onto the pile also before giving a
second zap.  Despairing of ever getting a magic marker I also drop my ten
blank scrolls on the pile.  After a few zaps they are scrolls of identify
so I pull them off.  A second scroll of enchant weapon also appears.

Once more I fall victim to the fast play syndrome.  I say 300 z s (the wand
is item "s" in my inventory) and pound the s key waiting for the last zap.
Alas, it comes and asks me for a direction.  The next press of the s key
has me polymorphed into a grey dragon, destroying my cloak of protection in
the process.  Now what do I do?  I cannot put on any armour.  My unicorn
horn doesn't cure this problem.  Will a potion of holy water restore me to
human form?  No.  And of course, not expecting to polymorph, I have long
since disposed of my ring of polymorph control.  Bugger.  There goes two
wishes at least.  I get a ring of polymorph control, then a wand of poly-
morph.  OH NO!  It won't let me polymorph into a human!  I try priest,
Jonathan the priest and a couple of other combinations before Nethack tells
me I have had enough tries and I become a Giant Mummy.  What if I remove my
mail?  DOUBLE OH NO!  I no longer have it!

Time to take serious stock.  What chances do I have now?  I can polymorph
back into a grey dragon and have most of my advantages.  My armour class
will not be -31 but something like -10.  With my ring of protection I can
get to -14 which is not too bad, but not exactly great.  I cannot walk on
water but I can levitate with my ring.  Is it worth continuing?  Of course!

Will I ever polymorph back into a human?  I do not know.  As you have
probably guessed, I am not an experienced polymorpher.  A long time ago I
discovered that quaffing holy water cures the fever which causes wererat
transfigurations and I have always regarded polymorphing as a BAD THING
even though I realize that other players do it routinely.  Maybe I haven't
played enough because I've never before had the means to transform AND to
control the transformation.  If I had not done so well in this game and
so did not have such a good chance of winning I'd be tempted to experiment
but right now my concern is how to recover from this catastrophe.

There are polymorph traps in the upper levels; I do remember there is one
in the maze on level 27.  I didn't mention it before because wearing grey
dragon scale mail one just ignores them.  Perhaps I should go back and try
uncontrolled polymorphs rather than use up the precious charges in my wand?
I just don't know but I have no better idea.  Out through the small maze,
up the stairs, up again and I am halfway across the dungeon when I return
to human form!  Whew!  Is this temporary or permanent?  At least I can put
on what is left of my armour.  I'm at AC -14 which my ring pushes down to
-18.  Not exactly wonderful at this stage of the game but not too horrible
either.  I have the chance to get some more grey dragon scale mail if I can
deal with the monsters on the castle level.  My main worry on that score is
that I do not have disintegration resistance.

Back down to the castle level I enter through the mercifully empty chambers
and, wearing my ring of levitation, traverse the corridor to expose the
trapdoors.  I can see a black and a blue dragon in the northern passage-
way and a black dragon in the southern one.  Also in the south-eastern
chamber the grey dragon I saw earlier is still wandering around.  I'm not
really sure how to deal with these fellows so in case I have to retreat in
a hurry I remove my ring of levitation and land between the passageways.
I search for and find the hidden doors and then take a step to the west
before kicking the doors open.  The blue dragon emerges first.  I take
another step west and a black dragon steps onto the square next to me.  I
am then blinded by a lightning flash but I do not take time to use my uni-
corn horn.  The black dragon next to me succumbs fairly quickly and I pre-
sume that disintegration blast which evaporates my ring of polymorph control
is from the other black dragon.  I step onto the black dragon corpse and
start hacking at the other dragons.  They are fighting each other so I do not
sustain much damage.  Now I use my unicorn horn to cure my blindness and my
tinning kit to make two tins of black dragon meat and one of blue.

The grey dragon did not participate in the melee so with 85 hit points left
I go after it.  I manage to kill it with over 30 hit points remaining.  I
zap the corpse with my wand of polymorph and don the skin.  My armour class
is now at a more respectable -23.

Well I guess I have recovered somewhat from the earlier disaster and there
are more good things in store.  I enter the armoury and there is a cloak of
displacement, a cloak of protection and a Hawaiian shirt there.  I don't
know which is better, displacement or of protection so I choose the latter.
I put on the Hawaiian shirt but as yet it does nothing for me.  It is time
to use some of those wishes.  I believe I have five left.  I ask for three
blessed scrolls of enchant armo(u)r and get one.  I still have several
scrolls of identify so I try a ruse.  I ask for a blessed magic marker which,
on identification, has a charge of 50.  I put on my ring of levitation and
my water-walking boots and head out to the moat.  I #dip six of my scrolls
of identify and between writing scrolls of charging and enchant armour end
up with

	a blessed +4 cloak of protection (being worn).
	a blessed +5 Hawaiian shirt (being worn).
	a blessed +5 pair of gauntlets of dexterity (being worn).
 	a +4 helm of telepathy (being worn).
	a blessed +5 pair of speed boots (being worn).
	a +6 gray dragon scale mail (being worn).
	a blessed +4 pair of water walking boots.

and, when wearing my ring of protection, an armour class of -46.  Not too
shabby!  I still have a magic marker (31) and a wand of wishing (2) which I
shall save for later.  

I am hungry now so I eat one of the tins of black dragon meat.  I feel firm!
I eat the blue dragon meat too but it doesn't tell me I'm shock resistant so
I look back through these notes and see that I already have that attribute.
(When did I get sleep resistance?  I don't remember that at all.)

Time to have a look at the underworld.  Back in the corridor and not wearing
my ring of levitation I drop through a trapdoor into hell.  A few quick
scuffles and I acquire several useless potions and wands and a couple of
cans of giant meat.  I'm just starting to struggle with this load so I eat
one can of giant meat and head upstairs to the castle level again with all
that lovely water in the moat.  I convert the potions to water and then to
holy water.  The wands I pile up and zap a few times with my wand of poly-
morph but nothing interesting happens so I leave all the wands there
(except for my wand of wishing, of course).  I have 10 potions of holy
water - probably more than I need - so I leave a couple here.  The reasoning
behind this is that the Wizard of Yendor is likely to curse stuff, including
my holy water.  Two potions of holy water will be enough to convert whatever
I have on my way back up.  I elect to drop the water in the passageway just
outside the northern moat where the potions should be relatively immune to
pilfering.  I notice that the gate on the north-eastern turret is locked and
I wonder about that until I move away a bit and realize that I have been
seeing a mimic masquerading as a closed door.

I also drop one of my two blessed luckstones (now identified).  After con-
sideration it seems unlikely that two are better than one.  My full inven-
tory is now:

	Weapons
	o - a blessed +4 broadsword named Stormbringer (weapon in hand).
	L - a +6 war hammer named Mjollnir.
	Armor
	d - a blessed +4 cloak of protection (being worn).
	p - a blessed +5 Hawaiian shirt (being worn).
	E - a blessed +5 pair of gauntlets of dexterity (being worn).
	F - a +4 helm of telepathy (being worn).
	G - a blessed +5 pair of speed boots.
	M - a +6 gray dragon scale mail (being worn).
	O - a blessed +4 pair of water walking boots (being worn).
	Comestibles
	f - 4 C-rations.
	g - 2 K-rations.
	q - a blessed tin of frost giant meat.
	t - a blessed tin of yellow dragon meat.
	Scrolls
	n - a scroll called remove curse.
	w - a blessed scroll of genocide.
	V - a scroll called enchant weapon.
	X - a blessed scroll called enchant weapon.
	Potions
	D - 7 potions of holy water.
	Rings
	m - a ring of conflict.
	x - a ring of levitation.
	y - a ring of regeneration.
	J - a +4 ring of protection (on left hand).
	Wands
	C - a wand of wishing (2).
	Tools
	a - a blessed +0 unicorn horn.
	K - a +0 pick-axe.
	S - a blessed tinning kit.
	W - a blessed magic marker (31).
	Gems
	b - a yellowish brown gem.
	h - a blessed luckstone.
	v - a green gem.

and I am at experience level 15 and getting those damned annoying messages
as my fingers glow various colours.  I presume the message about feeling
sensitive that I had a while back came as I reached experience level 15 and
meant that I had acquired the "warned" intrinsic.  I was too busy at the
time with other matters to pay it any attention.

I believe Stormbringer is not rustproof.  If I try enchanting it now it is
likely to evaporate.  I hope to find a rust trap and have it lose a point
before reading my blessed scroll of enchant weapon.  I still have to rust-
proof my helm of telepathy sometime too.

I am not sure what I should kill off with the blessed scroll of genocide.
Dragons perhaps?  Nagas?  None of those seems particularly dangerous now
so for the moment I elect to do nothing.  Pending another scroll of identify
I'll carry the gems around a bit longer, too.

I fall through the trapdoor again down to level 32.  I complete the mapping
of the level without finding a rust trap or a level teleporter so I climb
back up to the castle level and then up again.  On level 30 I do find a
black pudding which corrodes Stormbringer nicely when I attack.  I withdraw,
read my scroll of enchant weapon and am rewarded by a +6 Stormbringer.  I
wield Mjollnir now because I have yet to rustproof Stormbringer.

To get down to the depths of the dungeon I head in the opposite direction.
I can't find my level teleporters (did I have any unused ones?) until I get
back to level 24.  Then, taking off my cloak of protection and dragon skin
I teleport down to level 50 where I immediately trigger a land mine and am
unable to move for several turns.  I could see a blue dragon hovering in the
near distance but obviously there were walls in the way.

Foolishly, I am wielding Stormbringer and I stumble onto a rust trap and so
now I have a +5 sword rather than a +6 one.  Boo.

Since 50 is obviously a dry level and thus not the Wizard level I don't
bother to completely map the level and head upwards as soon as I find the
staircase.  On 49 a wraith leaves a corpse and on eating it I gain another
experience level.  I find a level teleporter here but I can't imagine a use
for it just now.

After exploring a bit and bashing a few monsters I can see some suspicious-
looking creatures in the middle of the level.  I suspect that this is a wet
level and, sure enough, after a while I work my way to the centre and see
a moat.  Nearby I encounter a cockatrice which I quickly dispatch.  Back at
the water's edge I change into my water-walking boots and walk around the
walls.  I see four monsters inside, a Vampire, a quasit, a hell-hound and a
devil.  Opening the wall I convert the quasit into a statue, then the devil
who is identified as "the invisible Geryon" and finally the hell hound.  I
pick up the Amulet of Yendor although I do not believe it is the real one.

I leave the cockatrice corpse inside Geryon's lair and go exploring further.
By now I have mapped over three quarters of the level.  Another cockatrice
hisses but succumbs to Mjollnir in two blows.  I remember that I am still
wearing my water-walking boots and change back into my speed boots.  I almost
get myself killed through carelessness.  There is another cockatrice nearby
but I stupidly attack a gelatinous cube.  Fortunately I don't get frozen for
very long.  If I had, the cockatrice would have had plenty of fun converting
me into a statue.

On level 48 I encounter an umber hulk and have the chance to rustproof my
sword.  I wield it and head towards the beast.  Unfortunately it is not
antagonistic so I un-wield Stormbringer before hitting the umber hulk with
my bare hands.  Now its gaze confuses me so I wield Stormbringer again and
read my scroll of enchant weapon.  Finally, a rustproof +5 sword.  Mind you,
after all this I wonder if Stormbringer has much to recommend it over
Mjollnir.  Many of the creatures in Hell are dead things and Stormbringer
has less effect on those.  Mjollnir seems to be a more effective weapon.
(Not that I propose to drop Stormbringer right now.)

This is another wet level and the keep at the centre is inhabited by a
vampire lord, a hell hound and an invisible devil called Baalzebub.  Since
Baalzebub and the hell hound are fighting each other I realize I am still
wearing my ring of conflict.  No wonder my food is going quickly.  By now
I am utterly convinced that my first Amulet of Yendor is a fake so I drop
it and pick up the one that is here, although I am pretty sure that is a
fake too.

Level 47 is dry and boring so after exploring only about half of it I climb
the stairs.  Level 46 is boring too and the wraith I killed didn't leave a
corpse.  It takes me a long time to find the stairs.   I leave my useless,
fake Amulet of Yendor behind.
  
Level 45 is the base of Vlad's tower.  I walk around the tower contemplating
all the beasts inside, stop outside the entrance, put on my ring of conflict
and kick down the door.

After disposing of the monsters I investigate the little chambers.  Most are
empty.  One has a lock pick which I don't really need and one has a blind-
fold which I don't need either.  On second thoughts I take the blindfold.
It may be useful for locating the Wizard of Yendor later, and, since he has
a habit of teleporting to the stairs, it might serve as a stair-locator too.

One of the traps in the little rooms is a level teleporter and I am tempted
to use it to go back down a couple of levels.  The reason for this is that
I am carrying a couple of useless scrolls and I'd really like a scroll of
identify.  It doesn't take long to go down and up again.  Back in the base
of Vlad's tower I climb the stairs and in one of the small rooms I find a
triangular amulet.  I am already carrying a pyramidal amulet and several
unidentified gems.  I make myself a blessed scroll of identify and read it.
I discover that my pyramidal amulet is an amulet of reflection and the one
I just picked up is an amulet of life saving.  I drop the amulet of re-
flection and put on the one of life saving.  Should I bless it?  What is the
difference between an amulet of life-saving in its cursed, normal and blessed
states?

The only other thing I identified was a topaz so I drop that and investigate
the other rooms.  One turns up another amulet - a cursed square one - so I
don't even bother with it.

Up on the top level I see lots of vampires, vampire lords and, of course,
Vlad the Impaler himself.  I have a blessed scroll of genocide with me and
I am tempted to get rid of all the vampires.  It seems to work except that
I'm not allowed to genocide Vlad.  Oh well, that's interesting, anyway.

Retrieving a thick spellbook from the chest in the first side-chamber I
try to read it but even with 18 and 18 for intelligence and wisdom I fail.
It must have been a worthwhile spell!

The chest in the second chamber yields a food ration and a cursed scroll of
identify whereas the third contains only some worthless gems and a coconut.

From the next three chests I get some scrolls of identify which allow me to
drop most of my gems as they are all semi-precious stones.  I end up with
one unidentified green gem and a bunch of useless potions and scrolls.  I
make myself a scroll of charging and use it on the magic marker but nothing
happens so I am able to drop the magic marker.  That is just as well as I
am having trouble carrying everything.  I have already abandoned three C
rations, my blindfold and a wand of digging.  Back at the base of Vlad's
tower I head for the stairs.  My load is still too heavy to climb but eating
a food ration enables me to climb.  No mucking around now, I use my wand of
digging to cut through all the walls along the northern extremity of the
dungeon and climb the stairs again.  On level 43 I stumble into a level tele-
port trap.  To save the trouble of hacking my way to the stairs I take off my
cloak of protection and dragon mail and take the quick way up to level 42.
That is a dry level and not very interesting so as soon as I find the stairs
I climb them.  The only thing I collected on 42 was an unidentified white gem.

On level 41 I encounter a hill giant and after eating its corpse my strength
is at 18/71.  This is also a dry level and after mapping roughly a third of
the level I find the stairs and climb them but I have to abandon my wand of
digging in order to do so.

Level 40 is dry but I find a wand of polymorph and use it on my potions and
scrolls.  I pull out a scroll of identify and a potion of gain level and
reach experience level 17.  At one stage I see a potion of confusion and a
scroll of enchant armour in the pile so I rustproof my helm of telepathy.
Another potion of gain level pushes my experience to 18 and I also extract a 
second scroll of identify from the pile.  I use up all the charges on the
wand of polymorph (except the hidden one) in the hope of getting a cursed
scroll of genocide but that doesn't happen.  I do finish up with three plain
scrolls of identify which I know I can convert to blessed ones whenever I
choose.  Picking up the rest of the potions I wander off.  I have failed to
notice that I am not wearing much armour - indeed, apart from my helm of
telepathy I am still naked.  Mistake!  I challenge a Minotaur and don't
watch my hit points.  Dead!  But wait!  My medallion glows and crumbles away.  
I am restored to life and health and quickly retreat to dress.  Whew!  Those
minotaurs are heavy beasts.  Two or three hits and my 125 hit points counted
for nothing!

It takes me a long time to find the stairs but before climbing I decide to
use a wish to get myself another amulet of life saving.  Seems like a rather
valuable piece of equipment!

I map most of level 39 before finding the stairs.  Level 38 is a wet level
so I convert my useless potions to holy water.  The keep at the centre of
the level is occupied by Asmodeus who is peaceful, and a hell hound who
probably isn't.  I use my pickaxe to open the wall.  As I enter the keep
I step on a squeaky board.  Asmodeus appears before me and demands 18 zork-
mids for safe passage.  I have 25 so I give him the 18 and he disappears,
muttering something about cowards.  After disposing of the hell hound I pick
up what is probably yet another fake Amulet and wander out towards the
stairs which I found on my way here. 

On level 37 I immediately get immobilized by standing on a land mine.  The
Wizard of Yendor appears with a whole host of nasty followers so I put on
my ring of conflict.  I survive the period of immobility and head for the
centre of the level.  On the way I encounter the Wizard of Yendor several
times and eventually manage to kill him.  I use my blessed tinning kit and
am then carrying a blessed tin of Wizard of Yendor meat.  Hmm.  I pick up
the REAL Amulet of Yendor and go looking for the stairs.  My idea is now to
get to the endgame as quickly as possible.

Confirmation that I have the real amulet is soon provided as bits of the
maze become mapped out for me.  It still takes me some time to find the
staircase.  On the way I discover a level teleporter and thinking to take
a quick trip to level 1 I take off my cloak and dragon skin and step onto
it.  All that happens is that I feel disoriented for a moment.

Every so often I notice that I am surrounded by a malignant aura.  Things
that I am carrying are losing enchantment and becoming cursed.  So far
nothing important has become cursed and I am still carrying two lots of
holy water - one parcel of four potions, another of two.  I have refrained
from combining them to ameliorate the risk of losing them.

On level 36 I don't gain much strength from eating a frost giant corpse -
just one point.  I have to map most of the level (aided by the Amulet) be-
fore I find the stairs.  On level 35 I have even more trouble.  By the time
I get to level 34 my dragon skin is cursed as is my ring of protection.
However I have found another blindfold and putting it on after a Wizard
attack reveals the location of the stairs.  It takes me a while to get there
though because I miss-teleport a couple of times.  I find the stairs on
level 33 very quickly and I am soon on the level below the castle.  My
attempt to climb is thwarted when I am surrounded by some sort of a glow
(can't remember the exact message and cannot recall it with control-P) and
I am returned to level 34.  Trying to climb to level 33 I see the message
again ... "A mysterious force surrounds you" ... and I am down to 37!  I
teleport to the stairs, climb and it happens again!  Now I am back on level
38!  Bloody hell!  I am close to the stairs so up to 37, teleport to the
stairs, up to 36.  I try teleporting but I just feel disoriented for a
moment and have to wait for a spontaneous teleport opportunity to get to
the stairs quickly.  I manage to get to level 35 just a short distance from
the staircase.  On 34 I am again close to the stairs but there is a wall in
the way.  Clobbering a nearby minotaur provides nourishment and a means to
tunnel through the wall without using the pickaxe.  Level 33 and one tunnel
and a spontaneous teleport finds me back at the stairs.  On level 32 again
I am ready to climb up to the castle level once more.  This time I manage it.
I put on my water-walking boots and retrieve my holy water from the northern
passageway.  Through the castle level I pause only to pick up a food ration
and a couple of lembas wafers.  I get a spontaneous teleport on level 30 so
I am up to level 29 in one turn.  I quickly reach level 24 then the Wizard
attacks with his hordes.  My ring of conflict helps although I have to dis-
pose of a couple of dragons myself.  The Wizard attacks me again on level
22 and steals the Amulet.  I get it back quickly enough because I know where
he went and I have to go there too.  I get to level 6 before he attacks me
again, several times.  He doesn't summon help but his attacks are vicious
and by the time I am ready to ascend to level 5 much of my equipment is
cursed, including my helm of telepathy, a potion of water, my dilithium
crystal, my pick-axe and my wand of wishing with its two charges left.  On
level 5 I visit the lawful altar and use some of my newly-charged potions
to uncurse my wand.  I don't know what I am going to use the wand for
because there doesn't seem to be anything that I need.  I don't bother un-
cursing my armour because I have no intention of taking it off anyway.
I uncurse my blindfold in case I need it later.  I drop my pick-axe and
my ring of levitation because I assume that they are now useless to me.
I have second thoughts about the pick-axe and retrieve it.  On level 2 I
encounter Rover and decide to take him along with me just for fun.  I feed
him a wumpus corpse which he devours hungrily.  I now have a use for my
wand of wishing.  I get a wand of polymorph and wave it at Rover but it
doesn't do me much good.  Rover is changed into a mimic, a kobold, a
zombie and finally a stone golem.  With nothing else to use the wand of
wishing for I try again.  I get another wand of polymorph and throw away
the wand of wishing.  Just as I get back to Rover he is eaten by a purple
worm.  Oh well. C'est la guerre.  I retrieve my wand of wishing (0).

On level 1 I am at last ready to tackle the endgame.  At this point I have

	Amulets
	 i - a blessed amulet of life saving (being worn).
	 q - the cursed Amulet of Yendor
	Weapons
	 o - a blessed +5 broadsword named Stormbringer (weapon in hand).
	 L - a +6 war hammer named Mjollnir.
	Armor
	 d - a blessed +4 cloak of protection (being worn).
	 p - a blessed +5 Hawaiian shirt (being worn).
	 E - a +5 pair of gauntlets of dexterity (being worn).
	 F - a cursed +4 helm of telepathy (being worn).
	 G - a blessed +5 pair of speed boots.
	 M - a +6 gray dragon scale mail (being worn).
	 O - a blessed +4 pair of water walking boots (being worn).
	Comestibles
	 u - 3 lembas wafers.
	 Q - 3 food rations.
	Scrolls
	 Y - 2 scrolls of identify.
	Potions
	 D - 3 potions of holy water.
	Rings
	 m - a cursed ring of conflict (on right hand).
	 y - a ring of regeneration.
	 J - a cursed +4 ring of protection (on left hand).
	Wands
	 C - a blessed wand of wishing (0).
	Tools
	 a - a blessed +0 unicorn horn.
	 K - a +0 pick-axe.
	 N - a blindfold.
	 S - a blessed tinning kit.
	Gems
	 h - a blessed luckstone.
	 v - an emerald.
	 P - a cursed dilithium crystal.

and my characteristics are:

   Jonathan the Canon        St:18/92 Dx:22 Co:17 In:18 Wi:18 Ch:18  Neutral
   Dlvl:1  G:7  HP:129(129) Pw:107(107) AC:-46 Xp:19/2582711 T:60496

I probably don't need the tinning kit so I leave that behind and ascend to
level zero.  I find myself in the southeast corner of another maze which I
map out.  It occupies the eastern third of the level and there is a corridor
running the full length from north to south on the western edge of the maze.
On the other side of the wall, towards the centre of the level, I can see
many monsters of various sorts.  I start searching from the north and quickly
discover a hidden door.  It opens easily into a small room populated with
rust monsters.  As they fight each other I wander around bashing them too
and they are soon a bunch of dead rust monsters.  To the west I can see lots
and lots of dragons.  I start searching the walls and find a door in the
south-western corner of the room which leads into a second room lightly
populated with a variety of monsters, including a very long worm.  None lasts
very long.  I discover another hidden door in the south-eastern corner of
this room.  Behind the wall I can see lots of nagas.  The door is locked so
I have to kick it open.  There are only five nagas and they succumb quickly.
I search in the south-western corner of this room and find another door.  I
know that behind it are eight dragons and a cockatrice so I hope I can get
inside the door.  However those dragons are crowding it so I may have to
fight them one at a time.

I do manage to get my foot in the door but the dragons don't seem to be too
keen on fighting each other.  Nevertheless they do not all attack me at
once either so I am able to deal with them.  Furthermore, I don't lose
anything to the disintegration blasts which the black dragons hurl at me.
I also have to fight a couple of hill giants, a cockatrice, a wraith and an
energy vortex.  There is a river across the centre of this room which seems
to stretch from south to north.  There is a bridge in the middle but to guard
against the possibility of drowning I take the precaution of changing into my
water-walking boots before clobbering the krakens which occupy the waters.

On the other side of the river I kill a couple of hill giants and then start
looking for a door on the western wall.  I find it quickly enough in the
north-western corner of the room.  Behind the wall I can see several owlbears
and a frost giant.  Of course when I step into the room they start fighting
each other.  The frost giant disposes of the owlbears and then succumbs to
my attack.  I search the southern wall of this room and find a hidden door.
Behind the wall I can see a host of ogres, an elf and an ettin.  The door is
locked so I kick it open.  The ogres are a bit hard to kill; they run away
and throw things at me.  After a while I manage to dispose of them and only
then realize that I am not wearing my speed boots.  In the next room trolls,
an Olog-Hai, a baluchitherium and a purple worm fight each other while I
make my way to the south-western corner and look for the door.  I kick it
open and find myself in another full-length corridor running north-south.
An opening off to the west leads to another maze.  The maze leads almost
directly to a dark room in the south-western corner of the level.  The room
is almost completely surrounded by water.  As I enter I am surrounded by
heavy-duty monsters: an ice troll, a red dragon, an ochre jelly, an umber
hulk and an invisible stalker.  After clearing the monsters I can see an
altar to Cron.  I sacrifice the corpse of the invisible stalker.  I pick
up the ice troll corpse and, returning to the altar make an #offer.  I
cannot remember the inventory letter for the ice troll corpse so I press
the "?" key.  I notice something strange.  Among the items which can be
offered are my amulet of life saving and the (cursed) Amulet of Yendor.
Is this the finale?  I offer the troll corpse and my sacrifice is accepted.
I sacrifice the rest of the corpses and go exploring again.  Without
venturing back into the maze I use my pick-axe to cut a passageway north
and discover two other water-bound rooms similar to the first, each con-
taining an altar, one to Set and one to Mitra.  There seems to be nothing
for me to do in these so I return to the first room and the altar to my
god.  My intention is to see what happens if I do sacrifice the Amulet of
Yendor.  It is cursed and I have no idea what the effect of offering a
cursed item will be.  Nearby in the pile of things I dropped so I could
carry the corpses is my holy water.  I elect to use two potions to bless
the Amulet of Yendor.  Then I #offer the Amulet.  I am bathed in radiance.
I am granted immortality.  I become a Demigod.  This seems to be the end
because now I am asked if I want my posessions identified.  I say yes but
I don't pay much attention.  I am asked if I want to see my intrinsics and
I am presented with a long list which I don't really bother to read.  I am
told that I scored about a million and a half points including some for
my gems and my amulet of life saving but no gold.  Finally the honour roll
shows me in 17th place.

So that is it?  Bit of an anti-climax, really. 
